dossier.design:
Run 2–3 evolvers: GEPA, ACE, and one code-level evolver (AHE-lite or A-Evolve). Use 2 cheap backbones, one of them open (Qwen-class), with 3 seeds or lineages each. Use a procedural tau-world as the main environment and BreakingWeb (519 paired tasks, 7 primitives, 4 layers) for a confirmatory subset. Score every archive candidate on a small intervened validation set. Correlate intervened vs clean validation scores with the held-out paired drop, the false-finish rate, cross-benchmark transfer, and the HDA residual. Evaluate every few generations to estimate per-primitive robustness slopes with a mixed-effects model (lineage random effects, k≥3 evaluation passes). Compare these arms at matched rollouts:
(i) clean evolution;
(ii) clean evolution plus robust selection, i.e. a min(clean, intervened) gate;
(iii) gate exposure to 3 primitive families with 4 held out;
(iv) the clean champion plus a generic "re-read state before finishing" instruction.
Add a matched-clean-accuracy control built from hand-written harnesses and early checkpoints. Pre-register two-sided, per-primitive hypotheses (H+ verification erosion vs H− inserted verification). Start with a pilot under $50: GEPA × 1 open model, 2 lineages × 8 generations, 2 gate families and 2 held-out families, to get the sign and variance.
